// How the engines render the camera of the botshare base, by the name it has
// in the description, whose optical frame places it: the Orbbec Gemini 336L
// at the base's front, measuring the depths the description's depth sensor
// gives it, the colour aligned to its depth.
//
// - fovy_deg: the depth field's 65 degrees high, of its 90 x 65
//   (openAMRobot/openamr-platform-sw at 69847ab7, the commit the description
//   is written from, ros2/src/openamrobot_description/config/sensor_profiles.yaml,
//   base_camera_link depth fov_vertical, from Orbbec's product page).
// - width, height and fps: a mode of this entry, 640 x 400 at 15 fps, half
//   each way of the depth's largest, 1280 x 800 at up to 30 fps (the same
//   file's width_max, height_max and frame_rate_max). botshare's software
//   sets no mode of the camera: the file says the rate on the robot is set in
//   the driver launch, and the repository holds none for it.
{
  cameras: {
    base_camera: {
      fovy_deg: 65.0,
      color: { width: 640, height: 400 },
      depth: { width: 640, height: 400 },
      fps: 15,
    },
  },
}
